<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN WALIBI GROUP LOSSES RISE IN 1996.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN WALIBI GROUP LOSSES RISE IN 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net loss		   179	vs	     10</p>
<p>    Sales			    2,524	vs	  2,668</p>
<p>    Operating profit		  22	vs	    201</p>
<p>    Pre-tax current loss	   125	vs profit    27</p>
<p>NOTE - The Walibi Group operates theme parks. It said visits</p>
<p>to its parks fell eight percent in 1996 against 1995 due to the</p>
<p>depressed economic climate and bad weather. It said it did not</p>
<p>plan to pay a share dividend on the 1996 results. The firm said</p>
<p>it had restated its 1995 results to conform with new accounting</p>
<p>standards. The effect of this new standard added 28 million</p>
<p>francs to the 1996 bottom line.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
